3 m above its rest Z, so it was lifted clear.\n- finger_joint efforts while held were 8-66, above the 0.05 floor and below each part's max_clamp_effort.\n- Grasp widths (from the executor's grasped phase, measured at the gripper) were within 0.0042 m of the declared width.\n\nStanding monitors, armed with clauses and registry thresholds:\n- bystander + base1 stationarity at disturbance_tolerance_m 0.02;\n- inactive-set stationarity, re-armed at each part change with references checked against the then-current rest poses;\n- clamp effort per held part;\n- in-hand slip at grasp_slip_tolerance_m 0.02.\nNone fired.\n\nAt run end the bystanders are within 0.0001 m of their start poses. base1 shifted 0.0029 m, which is within tolerance and consistent with seating contact. place_approach_line_green described its standoff as along the frame's local +Z. I checked: line_green_placement is world-aligned, so that was a vertical standoff 6 cm above the frame, not a sideways sweep.\n\nLimitations, stated rather than hidden:\n- Contact is not observable. Missed-grasp and contact were judged from the part rising with the TCP.\n- object_tcp_offset_m was evaluated as the change in offset after grasp (the slip monitor), because the absolute object-origin-to-TCP distance reflects grasp geometry.\n- The slip monitor's reference settle delay of 3 s is agent-chosen. It only sets when the reference is taken, and its description wrongly says 1 s.\n- Workspace observation was done by RGB looks at run start and run end, not continuously between steps. That is a coverage gap.\n\nThe end-of-run look shows a small red/orange block, upper centre of the image, that I did not see in the baseline look. It is recorded as observation obs-001-d5af404a (unlisted_object, low confidence). It does not coincide with any registered object's displacement and breaks no requirement.\n\nThe executor's claimed success and run_ended 'completed' agree with this independent measurement.","run_scope":true,"executor_terminal_status":"completed","findings_during_run":[],"recovered":false},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":35}
